他们意识到你无法逃避家人，那种仪式感——就像走过那场婚礼的历练，走过那条红毯，面对所有的目光，对吧——然后说我们是一个伴侣，而且我（你知道的）莉莉担心她会被马歇尔的家人痛恨，她觉得“我必须面对这一切”，我觉得这太棒了，这才是这一集真正聚焦的时候。

00:32:11.269 --> 00:32:18.549
I think I've said this quote on this podcast but there's that quote like that a person often meets their destiny on the road they took to avoid it.
我想我在这个播客里说过这句话，但有这样一句名言：一个人往往在为了逃避命运而选择的道路上与命运相遇。

00:32:19.430 --> 00:32:21.527
And it feels like this is like that's it.
感觉这就好像是……就是这样。

00:32:21.527 --> 00:32:22.038
That's it.
就是这样。

00:32:22.038 --> 00:32:22.549
That's it.
就是这样。

00:32:22.549 --> 00:32:23.049
Yeah.
对。

00:32:23.049 --> 00:32:35.579
They're trying to avoid their destiny of like not just marriage but having to live with the perhaps dissatisfaction of, you know, that like, it's not just that Lily feels like, oh, Marshall's family is mad at me.
他们试图逃避他们的命运，不仅是结婚，还要面对可能带来不如意的现实，你知道，这不仅是莉莉觉得“哦，马歇尔的家人对我很生气”。

00:32:35.579 --> 00:32:42.611
It's that Marshall is almost defensive like, because everyone's like, we don't want you to get your heart broken again.
而是马歇尔几乎带有防御性，因为每个人都说，我们不想让你再次心碎。

00:32:42.611 --> 00:32:46.157
Because boy, did he not have an easy time with that breakup?
因为天哪，他上次分手可一点都不容易。

00:32:46.157 --> 00:32:48.994
So there's people who are trying to protect him.
所以有些人是在试图保护他。

00:32:50.309 --> 00:32:58.757
But it also feels like in some ways, the judge and the ship captain function as the reminder that they're not getting out of this.
但这也让人觉得，在某种程度上，法官和船长起到了提醒作用，提醒他们是逃不掉的。

00:32:58.757 --> 00:32:59.991
Like, what is that?
就像，那是什么？

00:32:59.991 --> 00:33:01.226
Like, what is that?
就像，那是什么？

00:33:01.226 --> 00:33:06.230
Like, you can't, you're not going to be able to avoid the discomfort of this.
就像，你不能，你是无法逃避这种不适感的。

00:33:06.230 --> 00:33:08.204
And it's actually kind of brilliant.
而且这其实有点绝妙。

00:33:08.204 --> 00:33:15.829
Like, it's a great metaphor that we sort of stumbled into that says what you just said, which is they're literally in international waters.
就像，这是一个我们无意中想到的绝佳隐喻，它表达了你刚才所说的，也就是他们字面意义上身处国际水域。

00:33:16.630 --> 00:33:20.069
That's how far they're trying to run away from the thing they're trying to avoid.
他们为了逃避想要躲避的事情，跑得就是这么远。

00:33:20.069 --> 00:33:27.365
They're in international waters on the janky old ship captains, like boat, whatever that boat is actually used for.
他们在一艘破旧的老船长的船上，身处国际水域，不管那艘船到底是用来干什么的。

00:33:27.365 --> 00:33:30.283
I don't know if he's specified, but you can't.
我不知道他有没有明说，但你逃不掉。

00:33:30.283 --> 00:33:31.488
You can't run away.
你无处可逃。

00:33:31.488 --> 00:33:34.470
They're going to have to face it at some point.
他们总得在某个时刻去面对。

00:33:34.470 --> 00:33:40.150
How much further are they going to run farther than the Atlantic Ocean?
他们还能跑多远，比大西洋还远吗？

00:33:40.150 --> 00:33:45.395
And there's something nice about accepting their destiny and saying, we're going to be, it's still going to be great.
接受他们的命运并说“我们会，这依然会很棒”是一件很美好的事。

00:33:45.395 --> 00:33:46.695
It's still going to be great.
这依然会很棒。

00:33:46.695 --> 00:33:49.699
It's going to be great because we walked through fire to get there.
这之所以会很棒，是因为我们历经火海才走到这里。

00:33:49.699 --> 00:33:52.390
We walked through all of these things we're trying to dodge.
我们走过了所有这些我们试图躲避的事情。

00:33:52.390 --> 00:34:01.444
You know, it occurs to me that when a network says, give us 22 episodes, give us 24 episodes, because I'd say half the seasons we were getting 24 orders, right?
你知道，我突然想到，当一家电视台说，给我们22集，给我们24集，因为我要说有一半的季度他们给我们下达的是24集的订单，对吧？

00:34:01.444 --> 00:34:03.878
Like, I think more than not, more than not.
就像，我觉得大多数时候都是这样，超过半数。

00:34:03.878 --> 00:34:04.500
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:09.989
This was still 22 season two, but after that, that I think it became 24 until the strike usually.
第二季的时候还是22集，但那之后，我觉得基本上都变成24集了，直到编剧罢工为止。

00:34:09.989 --> 00:34:22.989
So in some ways that the ferocious pay, I just read that Dostoevsky wrote Brother's Caramatsov like for a magazine, like he would do monthly installments.
所以从某种意义上说，那种疯狂的节奏——我刚读到陀思妥耶夫斯基写《卡拉马佐夫兄弟》就像是为杂志写的，他按月连载。

00:34:22.989 --> 00:34:24.510
Each chapter was a month, right?
每一章是一个月，对吧？

00:34:24.510 --> 00:34:27.710
Yeah, Dickens too, a lot of the Dickens novels, yeah.
对，狄更斯也是，狄更斯的很多小说也是，对。

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:33.269
Shakespeare had produced three plays a season for a company that was depending on him to produce these plays.
莎士比亚一个季度要为一家指望他产出剧本的公司制作三部戏。

00:34:33.269 --> 00:34:38.670
I think sometimes deadlines are fantastic motivators for creativity, right?
我觉得有时候截止日期是激发创造力的绝佳动力，对吧？

00:34:38.670 --> 00:34:40.489
If you have all the time in the world, you might do nothing.
如果你拥有全世界的时间，你可能什么也做不成。

00:34:40.489 --> 00:34:55.449
But if someone's expecting this in their inbox or you better get moving, but there's something about the 22, 24 episode order that both has you lean into absurdity and like, okay, let's get them out of the bar.
但如果有人正等着把东西收进收件箱，或者你最好抓紧时间，不过22集或24集的剧集订单有一种魔力，它既能让你拥抱荒诞感，比如“好吧，让他们离开酒吧”。

00:34:55.449 --> 00:34:56.570
Let's get them out of the apartment.
“让他们离开公寓。”

00:34:56.570 --> 00:34:58.369
Let's, okay, Atlantic City.
“好吧，去大西洋城。”

00:34:58.369 --> 00:35:02.130
Let's have them go back to Minnesota or whatever.
“让他们回明尼苏达或者随便什么地方。”

00:35:02.130 --> 00:35:16.650
Some of that stuff can feel like fat, but some of it can actually force you to exercise different narrative muscles, you know, which I think is like, yeah, if this was a 10 episode, 12 episode season, you're not gonna have Atlantic City in here.
其中一些内容可能会显得像是赘肉，但其中一些确实能迫使你锻炼不同的叙事肌肉，你知道的，我觉得这就好像是，如果这是一部10集、12集的剧季，你是不会把大西洋城写进去的。

00:35:16.650 --> 00:35:17.489
We wouldn't do it.
我们不会这么做的。

00:35:17.489 --> 00:35:18.369
I was thinking the same thing.
我也是这么想的。

00:35:18.369 --> 00:35:20.929
It didn't really get you anywhere.
这其实并没有带你走向任何地方。

00:35:20.929 --> 00:35:22.449
You couldn't have skipped over.
你没办法跳过去。

00:35:22.449 --> 00:35:26.570
That's the sort of flaw of the episode and that's maybe why it was a more difficult rewrite.
这可以说是这一集的一个瑕疵，也许这也是为什么重写它会更困难的原因。

00:35:26.570 --> 00:35:35.879
It's really interesting to hear you say, I remember this one was like, five in the morning, this motherfucker comes around and comes out were shooting at 9 a.m.
听到你这么说真的很有意思，我记得这一集是这样的，早上五点钟，这个混蛋就过来了，然后我们早上九点开始拍摄。

00:35:35.879 --> 00:35:42.455
I think it's really telling that the episode itself you could lift it out and the story of the season works fine.
我觉得很说明问题的一点是，你可以把这一集单独抽离出来，整季的故事依然运转得很顺畅。

00:35:42.455 --> 00:35:44.375
But there's this emotional thing.
但这里面有一种情感层面的东西。

00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:46.877
There's emotional commerce happening there.
这里面发生了情感上的交流。

00:35:46.877 --> 00:35:55.547
There's something Marshall had to emotionally process that were showing the audience and I think it brings them into those characters, journeys more.
马歇尔有一些必须在情感上去消化的东西，我们把它展现给了观众，而且我认为这让他们更加融入了这些角色的心路历程。

00:35:55.547 --> 00:35:57.700
I really think the episode has value.
我真的觉得这一集很有价值。

00:35:57.700 --> 00:35:58.863
I like this episode.
我喜欢这一集。

00:35:58.863 --> 00:35:59.678
But it's true.
但这也是事实。

00:35:59.678 --> 00:36:02.937
I think it wasn't absolutely season plot crucial, right?
我觉得它对整季的主线剧情并非绝对关键，对吧？

00:36:02.937 --> 00:36:04.042
That's fair to say.
这样说很公允。

00:36:04.042 --> 00:36:05.089
It could lift out.
它是可以被抽离出来的。

00:36:05.090 --> 00:36:08.118
But there's something about two things.
但这里面有些关于两点的东西。

00:36:08.118 --> 00:36:14.407
One, the central idea of like, okay, we're acting like this is easier than it is.
第一，核心观念就像是，好吧，我们表现得这比实际情况要容易。

00:36:14.407 --> 00:36:24.190
But also the fact that Ted and Robin and Barney are along No matter if their families are there, that family's gonna be there.
但同时也是因为泰德、罗宾和巴尼无论如何都在一起，不管他们的家人在不在，那个大家庭都会在那儿。

00:36:24.190 --> 00:36:25.030
Yeah.
对。

00:36:25.030 --> 00:36:36.860
And it's also a little bit funny, like if you're always trying to create situations where the five of us can be together, a lot of that, one is like, they're best friends, right?
而且也有点好笑，如果你总是试图创造一种让我们五个人能聚在一起的情境，其中很大一部分原因，一是他们是最好的朋友，对吧？

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:37.860
Oh, they're best friends.
哦，他们是最好的朋友。

00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:43.300
The other is, you're actually obligated to put us all in the episode, like every episode, you know?
另一个原因则是，你其实有义务把我们所有人都安排进这一集里，就像每一集一样，你知道吗？

00:36:43.300 --> 00:36:48.579
So you have to create a context where we all like roll together.
所以你必须创造一个背景，让我们所有人都能一起行动。

00:36:48.579 --> 00:36:49.800
Yeah, that's right.
对，没毛病。

00:36:49.800 --> 00:36:50.679
That's right.
确实如此。

00:36:50.679 --> 00:36:59.159
And I think the Barney gambling thing and the intimation that Barney had this gambling addiction, it's very funny at the end of the boat where he's like, why can't I just do it a little?
而且我觉得巴尼赌博的那段情节，以及暗示巴尼有这种赌博成瘾的问题，在船的最后非常搞笑，当时他说，为什么我就不能稍微玩一下呢？

00:36:59.159 --> 00:37:09.199
And like he really, that was another weird element of Barney that we got to explore by thinking of Atlantic City, by thinking they're gonna go there and what is Barney gonna do in Atlantic City?
就像他真的——这是巴尼身上另一个诡异的特质，我们通过想到大西洋城，通过想象他们要在那儿以及巴尼在大西洋城会做什么，从而得以探索。

00:37:09.199 --> 00:37:12.280
Well, he's got a gambling addiction.
嗯，他有赌博成瘾。

00:37:12.280 --> 00:37:14.280
He's like the fonzi of Atlantic City.
他就像大西洋城的方兹（Fonzie）。

00:37:14.280 --> 00:37:16.039
Everyone seems to know him.
似乎每个人都认识他。

